        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Extract Key Metrics from Insight Document"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1774024109111"
          },
          "code": "EXTRACT_KEY_METRICS_FROM_INSIGHT_DOCUMENT",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1774336924902",
          "id": "1774098593768",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774098593768_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an information extraction assistant.\n\nYou will be given:\n1) DATA: output of a RAG document tool. It may contain:\n   - a human-readable summary in DATA.value\n   - the actual extracted spreadsheet text in DATA.supportingChunks[].textChunk\n\n2) INPUT: JSON from the REST payload. The product name may be available as:\n   - INPUT[\"Product Name\"]\n   - INPUT.payload[\"Product Name\"]\n\nTASK\n- Use DATA.supportingChunks[].textChunk as the primary source of truth.\n- Find the single best matching record where:\n  the sheet field \"Product\" equals the input product name, case-insensitive and trimmed.\n- A record block means the \"Product\" row and the related rows/fields that belong to that same product until the next Product row, next product block, or end of chunk.\n\nEXTRACT these fields from the matched record block:\n- expectedMargin from \"Expected Margin\"\n- expectedDiscount from \"Expected Discount\"\n- entitlementUsage from \"Entitlement Usage\"\n- overallAverageUtilizationPercent from \"Overall Average Utilization %\"\n- comparisonPeriodLengthEach from \"Comparison Period Length (Each)\"\n- currentPeriodAverageUtilizationPercent from \"Current Period Average Utilization %\"\n- previousPeriodAverageUtilizationPercent from \"Previous Period Average Utilization %\"\n- usageTrend from \"Usage Trend\", only if an explicit value is present\n\nRULES\n- Do not guess. Only extract values present in the same matched record block.\n- Do not mix values from other product records or unrelated blocks.\n- If no product match is found, set matchFound=false and all extracted fields to null.\n- If a field label is present but its value is blank/missing, return null for that field.\n- For percentage fields, return the numeric value only. Example: \"30%\" -> 30.\n- Do not convert percent scale. Example: if the source says \"0.30\", return 0.30, not 30.\n- For comparisonPeriodLengthEach, preserve the source text. Example: \"90 days\".\n- Output must be VALID JSON ONLY.\n- Do not return markdown.\n- Do not return explanations outside the JSON.\n\nDATA:\n{{$context.$nodes.INSIGHT_DOCUMENT.$output}}\n\nINPUT:\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.payload}}\n\nReturn exactly this JSON structure:\n\n{\n  \"inputProductName\": string,\n  \"matchFound\": boolean,\n  \"matchedProductName\": string|null,\n  \"expectedMargin\": number|null,\n  \"expectedDiscount\": number|null,\n  \"entitlementUsage\": string|null,\n  \"overallAverageUtilizationPercent\": number|null,\n  \"comparisonPeriodLengthEach\": string|null,\n  \"currentPeriodAverageUtilizationPercent\": number|null,\n  \"previousPeriodAverageUtilizationPercent\": number|null,\n  \"usageTrend\": string|null\n}\n\nCRITICAL RULE:\nAfter locating the matching Product record block, extract all metrics ONLY from that same block. If a metric is not present in that same block, return null for that metric even if it appears elsewhere in DATA.\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Assign Default Values"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1774023622252"
          },
          "code": "ASSIGN_DEFAULT_VALUES",
