        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Risk Summary"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776670852462"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_RISK_SUMMARY",
          "id": "1776670384090",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776670384091_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an enterprise reporting assistant.\n\nAnalyze the input array of parts[] and return strict JSON only.\n\nInput:  \n{{$context.$nodes.RENEWALRISKASSESSMENTENGINE.$output.result}}\n\nTask:\n1. Read parts[].\n2. Find the objects where payload.MetricUnit is exactly:\n   - \"Financial Risk Level\"\n   - \"Churn Risk Level\"\n3. Treat payload.MetricExplainability as JSON, even if it is a quoted string. Parse it before using it.\n4. For each MetricUnit, use the latest record if multiple exist (based on available timestamp fields if present).\n5. Generate short, factual, business-friendly summaries.\n6. Return strict JSON only.\n\nRules:\n- Do not invent data.\n- Use only the matching part for each MetricUnit.\n- If any required field is missing, null, or not parseable, explicitly say it was not provided.\n- Include exact values where available (scores, %, weights).\n- Do NOT make assumptions or add “likely”, “appears”, or inferred statements.\n- Do NOT add filler sentences when data is missing.\n- Keep summaries concise, clear, and executive-friendly.\n\nData handling:\n- Prefer explicit fields in payload first (e.g., score, classification).\n- If not available, use values from parsed MetricExplainability only if explicitly present.\n- Do not derive or infer values unless clearly defined in the data.\n\nFinancial summary rules:\n- Mention the financial risk level from payload (e.g., classification). If missing, say it was not provided.\n- Mention the financial score if present; otherwise use explainability financialRiskScore if available; otherwise say it was not provided.\n\nMargin driver:\n- Include expected margin, actual margin, and margin variance ONLY if all are available.\n- If margin data is missing or incomplete, say: \"margin data was not provided\".\n- Do NOT infer margin status (no “on target” / “below target”) unless explicitly supported by values.\n\nDiscount driver:\n- Include discount percent ONLY if available.\n- State whether discount is within or outside policy ONLY if both discount value and policy threshold are present.\n- If discount data is missing or incomplete, say: \"discount data was not provided\".\n\n- Provide a driver explanation strictly based on available margin and discount data only.\n\nChurn summary rules:\n- Mention the churn risk level from payload. If missing, say it was not provided.\n- Mention the churn score if present; otherwise use explainability churnRiskScore if available; otherwise say it was not provided.\n\nDrivers:\n- Use explainability weights ONLY if available:\n  - Include usage weight and sentiment weight if present.\n  - If sentiment weight = 0, explicitly say sentiment is not factored.\n  - If usage weight = 0, explicitly say usage is not factored.\n- If both weights are missing or not parseable, say: \"churn driver data was not provided\".\n- Do NOT infer causes, trends, or relationships beyond explicitly provided data.\n\nOutput requirements:\n- Return strict JSON only.\n- Do not return markdown.\n- Do not add explanations outside the JSON.\n- Do not add extra top-level fields.\n- Return exactly this structure:\n\n{\n  \"summariesByMetricUnit\": {\n    \"Financial Risk Level\": \"string\",\n    \"Churn Risk Level\": \"string\"\n  }\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"summariesByMetricUnit\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"Financial Risk Level\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"Churn Risk Level\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"summariesByMetricUnit\"]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Merge Summary into Parts",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const engineOut = $context.$nodes.RENEWALRISKASSESSMENTENGINE.$output.result || {};\nconst parts = Array.isArray(engineOut.parts) ? engineOut.parts : [];\n\nconst llmOut = $context.$nodes.GENERATE_RISK_SUMMARY.$output || {};\nconst summaries = llmOut.summariesByMetricUnit || {};\n\nconst safeJsonParse = (s) => {\n  try { return JSON.parse(s); } catch (e) { return null; }\n};\n\nfor (const p of parts) {\n  const unit = p?.payload?.MetricUnit;\n\n  if (unit === \"Financial Risk Level\" || unit === \"Churn Risk Level\") {\n    const expl = safeJsonParse(p?.payload?.MetricExplainability) || {};\n\n    const summary = summaries?.[unit];\n    if (typeof summary === \"string\" && summary.trim() !== \"\") {\n      expl.summary = summary.trim();\n      p.payload.MetricExplainability = JSON.stringify(expl);\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n// IMPORTANT: return object with parts to match your output spec / downstream\nreturn { parts };"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1774247818375"
          },
          "code": "MERGE_SUMMARY_INTO_PARTS",
          "id": "1776670852462",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        }
      ],
